{"_id":"68a7360d8ec3d8323af12371","nodeId":"qSAdfaGUfn8mtmDjHJi3z","roadmapSlug":"backend","createdAt":"2025-08-21T15:06:53.149Z","description":"# ACID\n\nACID represents four database transaction properties: Atomicity (all-or-nothing execution), Consistency (valid state maintenance), Isolation (concurrent transaction separation), and Durability (permanent commit survival). These principles ensure reliable data processing and integrity in database systems, crucial for financial and e-commerce applications.","resources":[{"type":"book","title":"Database System Concepts - Silberschatz, Korth, Sudarshan","url":"https://db-book.com/","_id":"6a7588bab0650226a5eb44d8"},{"type":"official","title":"PostgreSQL Tutorial on Transactions","url":"https://www.postgresql.org/docs/current/tutorial-transactions.html","_id":"6a7588bab0650226a5eb44d9"},{"type":"article","title":"What is ACID Compliant Database?","url":"https://retool.com/blog/whats-an-acid-compliant-database/","_id":"6a7588bab0650226a5eb44da"},{"type":"video","title":"ACID Explained: Atomic, Consistent, Isolated & Durable","url":"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=yaQ5YMWkxq4","_id":"6a7588bab0650226a5eb44db"}],"updatedAt":"2026-08-07T07:26:50.654Z","lessonPacks":[],"paidResources":[{"_id":"6a5e04ddfb5fcb94d041699b","title":"roadmap.sh - Master SQL","partner":"roadmap.sh","type":"course","url":"https://roadmap.sh/courses/sql"},{"_id":"6a5e04ddfb5fcb94d04169c3","title":"Scrimba - Backend Developer Career Path","partner":"Scrimba","type":"course","url":"http://scrimba.com/the-backend-developer-path-c0tbi0l98f?via=roadmap"}],"contribution":"https://github.com/kamranahmedse/developer-roadmap/tree/master/roadmaps/backend/content/qSAdfaGUfn8mtmDjHJi3z.md"}
